<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $46.2 mln March 4.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $46.2 mln March 4.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $46.2 million surplus on March 4 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MARCH 4</p>
<p>Exports: $188 million</p>
<p>Imports: $132.7 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $142.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $151.3 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $46.2 million</p>
<p>MARCH DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $416.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $325.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $487 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $ 294.2 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $283.2 million ((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485415))</p>
</text>
